:Does anyone know if the CPU fan, at the front of the case just in front of
:the CPU heatsink, is a variable speed thermostatically-controlled unit in
:the AS 255?

  Yes, this system typically uses a two-speed temperature-controlled fan.

  If you have one of these systems -- and like most any other system with 
  a cooling fan -- periodically check for and clean off any grunge that 
  might have built up in the fan intake area -- in the case of the 
  AlphaStation 255 series, you can easily pop off the top and front covers 
  and get at any grunge that has built up on the metal grillwork located 
  immediately in front of the fan.  This metal grillwork is directly behind 
  the plastic grillwork visible at the front of the system enclosure.

