>:
>Where?  I'd be very happy to have ANY working version of EMACS for
>VMS 7.1 on an Alpha, even if it's only for some editing.  About a year
>ago I wasted a week trying to build from the VMS source package; as
>far as I can tell, it simply can't be done.

It can but not without *great* pains.  I have a working 19.28 as far as I
can tell.  I'm not an Emacs power user by any stretch of the imagination,
so I'm not certain all of the functionality is there.  I've been trying to
build a V20.?? with great great difficulty.  One of the problems is that
none of the 19.28 mods for VMS were ever introduced into the Emacs base-
line.  The psycho HAVE_mumbledefritz CONFIG.H builder (CONFIGURE.COM) is
also can of very slimey and disgusting worms.  

One of the biggest problems is that you cannot seem to pick up a build
where it fails.  I need to clean out all of the build targets, make any
changes to fix the problem causing the build to breakdown and then, re-
build.  You whittle away at it one stupid C bugger at a time and there
are plently of them for whittling.  I recently (very recently) setup to
use a rooted logical which points to an empty directory tree and to the
original source tree.  Builds still fail but I can more easily weed out
the built files for deletion.

One of the big problems with the Emacs build is its reliance on the C
compiler's production of intermediate output of preprocessor directives.
This is a kludged up bit of claptrap and makes fixing the bugs nearly
impossible.   Only the unix mindset could have devised such a mess.

