BSD Bob the old greybeard BSD freak <bobkeys@weedcon1.cropsci.ncsu.edu> writes:

>Can someone point me to any information as to what exactly a
>DEC InfoServer 150 is?  A websearch did not turn up much except
>for some references to it.  I am curious as to what the actual
>specs on the machine are.

it's been several years and i'm sure someone more knowledgeable on the
newsgroup will popup with details.

that said, from what i remember, the IS150 is a VAX based piece of gear
housed in a BA42 like case.

basically it was used as a sort of server which could provide sharing of
resources, e.g cdrom towers, and also be used to boot VXT xterminals.

it could probably also be used to share disk - we never used it for that.


it was superseded by the infoserver 1000 i believe which came in
much newer packaging (e.g support for BAXXX chassis).

i still have a IS150 sitting in the garage (seemed a shame to see it
thrown out).  it appears to have between one and three scsi buses - or
at least connectors, BNC ethernet and a few serial ports.   i think i
also have some VXT software cdroms for it.

regards,

-jason


