Hello y'all,

I want to configure a DEC 3000/300 for serial console, and access
the console from another computer. The machine must auto-boot.

I tried an exhaustive search on the 'net (that means: I got
exhausted ;-) ) and found not enough UI. The OpenVMS FAQ doesn't seem
to cover this topic.

What happens:

I have a DEC 3000/300 (it came with VMS) from which I have
disconnected the keyboard and the mouse. The machine displays the POST
messages on the frame buffer screen, until it can't detect keyboard 
and mouse, it displays a related error message, switches to serial
console (until now everything is OK), and refuses to auto-boot (due
to the POST error). Some FAQ suggested toggling jumper 3 on the
mainboard in order to activate the serial console, but that has no
effect (apparently). Same for W1. The instructions for a 3000/600 do
not apply to the /300.

I have made some loopback connector for the mouse/keyboard port,
which connects TX to RX for both mouse and keyboard. This connector
made the POST errors on a DECstation 5000/120 go away, so it seems to
work. On the DEC 3000/300, still "no keyboard" is reported, but the
POST finishes without an error, the machine does not switch to serial
console (which is bad), and happily continues to boot from disk
(which is good ;-) ). BTW: the 'console' NVRAM environment variable
(as known from DECstations) does not work any more.

Another problem with serial consoles:
On both DECstation and DEC 3000 (when using a null modem cable
connected to a PC), I cannot send any characters to the serial console
when the PROM monitor is active, only when the OS (e.g. NetBSD) is
active. I tried with dip and cu on Linux, and with the first, I even
can see the PROM monitor's output.

To summarize this lengthy text: How do I make serial consoles usable
on DEC 3000/300 machines?

Bye (and thanks in advance)
Michael
