I didn't want to turn this into a tirade on child rearing.  Her "threat"
to pull all my wires was obviously a statement of her disagreement of my 
method of maintaining control over her use of the PeeCee.  I really don't
think that Boot Camp is necessary.  She's generally fairly obedient.  She
is at that age where she is testing the envelope of my authority.  She is
also a teenage girl which -- and I will never understand this not having
ever been a teenage girl -- seems to mean that the telephone is as vital
to life functions as breathing. 


>When I was younger, folks I "grew up" with were told by their parents
