I looked at my stuff at home and found:
The single drive cable is PN 17-02212-01 Rev A01 (From a model 38)
The dual drive cable is PN 17-02296-01 Rev B01 (From a model 20)
The three drive cable is PN 17-02439-01 Rev A01 (Don't know what system it came
from.)

The single and dual drive cables are two 50 conductor ribbon cables, and are a bit
short and not very flexible.  The three drive cable uses normal, non-ribbon, cable
and is a lot longer and a lot  more flexible.

I think the model 38 uses the same BA42-A enclosure as the model 30.  The two
drive cable listed above is used in a BA42-B, with one drive mounted above the
other.  I don't know if it's long enough to use with two drives mounted next to
one another, as in the BA42-A enclosure.  The three drive cable would be your best
choice.

Since the SCSI bus is terminated on the SCSI controller board, the internal drives
should not be terminated.  The external connector is not SCSI-3.  It's just a SCSI
narrow bus with a non-standard connector.  If you don't have any external drives
the non-standard external terminator should be connected, but I've seen systems
run just fine without one.

