Robert DiRosario wrote:
> Does it matter which memory board is connected to which connector on the
> controller board?  Does the controller need to be installed before or
> after the memory cards (in the Q-bus) or does that not matter?

The three connector cable goes from J4 on the
base module (M7169) to each J2 on the 4-plane
modules (M7168).

One of the two connector leads goes from J1 
on the base module to J1 on the
first 4-plane module (i.e. the middle one
on the 3-connector lead) and the other
two connector lead goes from J2 on the
base module to J1 on the other 4-plane
module.


> I didn't expect to find dip switches on the board.  What are they for?

The switches S1-S3 select address lines 3,2,1 of
the I/O page CSR. S4 is unused. (0=On, 1=Off).


> Can I put more than one QDSS board set in a single VAX?

I don't think so.

Antonio

