  14th ANNUAL INTERNATIONAL INTERNET & SOFTWARE QUALITY WEEK 2001

                    <http://www.qualityweek.com>
                     29 May 2001 - 1 June 2001
                   San Francisco, California  USA

o  Registration.  For immediate QW2001 registration go to:
      <http://www.qualityweek.com/QW2001/register.phtml>

o  Tutorials.  Hear from a dozen experts in their topics in full-day
   or half-day tutorials:
     > Mr. Gualtiero Bazzana (ONION, S.P.A) "Web Testing Techniques
       and Tools (D1) (D2)"
     > Mr. Ross Collard (Collard and Co.) "Test Estimating (F1)"
     > Mr. Bill Deibler (Software Systems Qaulity Consulting)
       "Making the CMM Work: Streamlining the CMM for Today's
       Projects and Organizations (B2)"
     > Mr. Thomas Drake (Integrated Computer Concepts, Inc ICCI)
       "The Quality Challenge For Network Based Software Systems
       (G1)"
     > Mr. Tom Gilb (Result Planning Limited) "Software Inspection
       For The Internet Age: How To Increase Effect And Radically
       Reduce the Cost (A1) (A2)"
     > Dr. Cem Kaner (Florida Institute of Technology) "Teaching
       Testing: A Skills-Based Approach (F2)"
     > Mr. Ed Kit (SDT Corporation) "Establishing a Fully Integrated
       Test Automation Architecture (G2)"
     > Dr. Edward Miller (eValid, Inc.) "Client-Side WebSite Testing
       (E2)"
     > Dr. John Musa (Consultant) "More Reliable Software Faster And
       Cheaper (C2)"
     > Mr. Robert Sabourin (AmiBug.Com) "Getting Started --
       Stressing Web Applications: Stress Early -- Stress Often
       (E1)"
     > Dr. Norman Schneidewind (Naval Postgraduate School) "A
       Roadmap To Distributed Client-Server Software Reliability
       Engineering (C1)"
     > Mr. Erik Simmons (Intel Corporation) "Writing Good
       Requirements (B1)"

o  Keynote Talks.  Seven seasoned professionals from various sectors
   of industry form a great lineup of exceptional keynote speakers:
     > Mr. Thomas Drake (Integrated Computer Concepts, Inc ICCI)
       "Riding The Wave -- The Future For Software Quality"
     > Dr. Dalibor Vrsalovic (Intel Corporation) "Internet
       Infrastructure: The Shape Of Things To Come"
     > Mr. Hans Buwalda (CMG) "The Three "Holy Grails" of Test
       Development"
     > Mr. Dave Lilly (SiteROCK) "Internet Quality of Service (QoS):
       The State Of The Practice"
     > Ms. Lisa Crispin (Tensegrent) "The Need for Speed: Acceptance
       Test Automation in an eXtreme Programming Environment
       (QWE2000 Best Presentation)"
     > Dr. Linda Rosenberg (GSFC NASA) "Independent Verification and
       Validation Implementation at NASA"
     > Mr. Ed Kit (SDT Corporation) "Test Automation -- State of the
       Practice"

o  Parallel Presentation Tracks. Over 60 presentations in six
   parallel tracks:
     > Technology: New software quality technology offerings, with
       emphasis on Java and WebSite issues.
     > Management: Software process and management issues, with
       special emphasis on WebSite production, performance, and
       quality.
     > Internet: Special focus on the critical quality and
       performance issues that are beginning to dominate the
       software quality field.
     > Applications: How-to presentations that help attendees learn
       useful take-home skills.
     > QuickStart: Special get-started seminars, taught by world
       experts, to help you get the most out of QW2001.
     > Vendor Technical Track: Selected technical presentations from
       leading vendors.

o  Panel Sessions.  Pick industry experts' brains at three panel
   sessions:
     > Ask The Experts!  Chaired by Nick Borelli, supported by an
       interactive WebSite to collect the most-asked questions:
          <http://msoffweb.rte.microsoft.com>
     > How DO You Test Internet Software?  Chaired by Brian
       Lawrence.
     > How Will the Internet Affect Software Quality?  Chaired by
       John Musa.

o  Exhibitors:  Here's the lineup of exhibitors for QW2001:  Amphora
   Quality Technologies, Atesto Technologies, Inc., Butler
   Technology Solutions, Compuware, eTesting Labs, eValid, IEEE,
   LogiGear Corporation, McCabe & Associates, Microsoft Corporation,
   OCLC, Polyspace Technologies, Princeton Softech, QualityLogic,
   Inc., Reasoning Systems, Sesame Technology, Software Development
   Technologies, Software Research, Software SETT Corporation,
   Spherion, STQE, TeamShare, TechExcel, TechWeek, Tescom (Formerly
   AZOR), TestQuest, Vanteon, VeriTest.

o  Birds of Feather Sessions (BOFSs).  Organizer Mark Wiley has
   assembled a great lineup of BOFSs for QW2001:
     > Life as a New Test Manager, Moderated by Johanna Rothman
     > Creating a Curriculum for Software Testing, Moderated by Cem
       Kaner
     > Managing Requirements in Internet Time, Moderated by Brian
       Lawrence
     > Rapid Testing Without Sacrificing Software Quality, Moderated
       by Eric Patel and Nancy Landau
     > Extreme Programming (XP) Testing Practices, Moderated by Lisa
       Crispin
     > What are the "Holy Grails of Testing", Moderated by Hans
       Buwalda and Hung Nguyen
     > Handling Sticky Situations in Testing, Moderated by Elisabeth
       Hendrickson
     > Performance, Load and Stress Testing, Moderated by Ross
       Collard
     > Streamlining the Software CMM for Today's Projects and
       Organizations Moderated by Bill Deibler
   For details see:
      <http://www.qualityweek.com/QW2001/bofs.phtml>

o  SF Giants' Baseball Game.  Join QW2001 attendees in special
   reserved sections to see the Western Division race between the
   two top contenders, the SF Giants and the Arizona Diamondbacks.
   Will Barry Bonds hit another homer?  Join the excitement on
   Wednesday evening, 30 May 2001, in San Francisco's world-famous
