:series.,.

  The SRM console, OpenVMS, and Tru64 UNIX are not supported on the -a 
  series.

  Please check the OpenVMS FAQ, sections ALPHA22 and ALPHA23.

  Various of the -a series boxes do have hardware-level differences.  Two 
  common examples of where the hardware and software were incompatible are 
  with the PCI bridge chips and with the particular Pyxis chip interface 
  and implementation -- certain of the -a series hardware boxes just won't 
  work well with OpenVMS.  (IIRC, the 433a was one such box.)

  That said, I am aware of OpenVMS hobbyists that have successfully booted 
  OpenVMS on at least some of the -a series boxes.  If you have valid
  hobbyist licenses and you do want to try this, use the current firmware 
  and use only the PCI I/O widgets that are supported by OpenVMS.


