Paul Repacholi wrote:
> 
> The long roll-over time for the 1GHz chips from the GSs down to the DS
> boxen implies less than wonderfull things about yield though. 

Low CPU chip yield could be the or a cause of long roll-over time, but
so could several other factors, including:  not enough fast SRAM chips
for on-board caches, not enough ASIC folks to upgrade support chipsets,
not enough verification folks to test the upgraded support chipsets,
not enough module designers to upgrade PWBs, not enough signal integrity
folks to validate upgraded modules, not enough lab folks to do system
integration testing and agency certification, not enough firmware folks
to upgrade console support, not enough software folks to add and test
support for the faster CPUs/modules/systems, not enough marketing folks
to write claims that faster CPUs are usefully faster, not enough benchmark
folks to prove that faster CPUs are usefully faster, etc.

Having a better CPU is not enough; it takes a village to raise a platform.
-- 
Cheers, Bob


