Hello,

I have recently acquired, in non-working order, an MTI
Infinity 1525 DLT autoloader. On closer inspection,
this turned out to be a rebadged DEC drive (hence my
inquiries here). The DLT2000 unit inside the drive is a
DIGITAL Model TH4XC; the autoloader as a whole has
the Digital part no. TH4CA-EC

Symptoms are that the drive powers up OK, starts its POST,
but then stops. All the lights on the front of the unit
light up steady bar two (the Magazine Fault and Loader
Fault lights remain unlit):

    - Power On
    - Write Protected
    - Tape In Use
    - Use Cleaning Tape
    - Density Override
    - 2.6, 6.0, 10.0 and Compress
    - Eject, Load/Unload and Slot Select
    - All slot lamps.

If I open up the unit and swing the front open, the
following lights are FLASHING on the internal DLT2000
buried inside:

    - Unlabelled light hidden behind front bezel sticker
      just above 2.6GB light.
    - 2.6
    - 6.0
    - 10.0
    - Compress
    - Density Override

The following lights are UNLIT (note: this is on the
internal drive):

    - Write Protected
    - Tape In Use
    - Use Cleaning Tape

The Operate Handle light is ON (steady green). You can
manually operate the handle and load and unload tapes,
but the autoloader doesn't work at all - no eject, unload
or slot select.

The unit cannot be seen on the SCSI bus either.

I suspect this might be bad firmware (it was not operated
for over a year prior to its failure, and worked fine
before being "retired" - when next switched on, it showed
this behaviour.)

I picked up the DLT2000/2500/2700 user manual from
Quantum's website, where it discusses the firmware upgrade
procedure. However, the unit will not respond when I hold
down the Load/Unload button on the front of the autoloader
BUT will respond and request a firmware update tape if
I hold down the Unload button on the internal tape drive.

So, my questions are:

    - Does anyone know if this is a firmware problem?
    - Will everything break horribly if I try the
      firmware update using the INTERNAL drive (since the
      autoloader panel appeats to be refusing requests
      to perform a firmware update)? P.S - of course,
      I mean update the firmware with the correct DLT27xx
      firmware! Not the DLT2000 firmware!
    - If it's not a firmware problem, any idea what it is?
      No obvious mechanical problems, stuck cartridges,
      bits of broken plastic or tape, etc.
    - Failing all that, does anyone know where I can get
      a service manual? Preferrably for free as it's not
      worth wasting much money trying to fix this, because
      if it needs any parts, Quantum won't sell them to
      you...

Thanks for any insights you can provide,
Malcolm.

