>A lot of bugs??? What kind of bugs? I'm about to put 4.0d on my 3000/400
>at home.  It's a Turbochannel system, so Tru64 is out.

I believe the DEC 3000s are supported through V5.0A and the supporting
code is still present in V5.1.  I think the name change from Digital
UNIX to Tru64 UNIX was around V4.0F.  If you can get it, V4.0G is probably
a better choice than V4.0D.

>
>Is there a size limit to the root partition?

2 TB I think.  As as for any other AdvFS or UFS file system.

>I have an RZ29, can I just use a single partition for anything?

I wouldn't.  This was probably never tested.  My typical minimal
configuration is root on A, swap on B and combined /usr and /var
on whatever is left.  128 MB is sufficient for a V4 root.  If
you only have one disk you need to size the page/swap space
for the amount of virtual memory you expect to use.  If you
have multiple disks, consider spreading the space across them
fairly evenly.

>I don't recall what version of firmware I have.

Kits include the firmware CDROM for suitable for that version.
A badly out of rev. DEC 3000 will need multiple firmware kits
to get you upgraded.  I had a 3000 Model 500 that hadn't been
upgraded since it was new and the most current kits couldn't
touch the old firmware.

