In article <3AEED897.2FF7A9AE@gsfc.nasa.gov>, Robert DiRosario <robert.j.dirosario.1@gsfc.nasa.gov> writes:
> Will a VAX 3520 work in a "normal" Q-bus box like a BA213 or BA440 or a
> rack mount version of these or does it require a nonstandard backplane?
> 
The 3520 has a non-standard backplane. The 3520 uses a write-back cache
bus called Mbus. It uses L-series modules and the backplane is a
special one. There's a bus bridge (actually, a couple of them depending
on your requirements) between Mbus and Qbus; the three(?) leftmost slots
of the backplane are Qbus slots, then a special slot for the Qbus
adapter, and then Mbus slots for the rest of the backplane.
